✅ How to Make List Thread-Safe:
----------------------------------------------------------
There are 3 common ways:
1. Using Collections.synchronizedList() (Most common)
2. Using CopyOnWriteArrayList (Best for multi-threading)
3. Using Vector (Old way)
------------------------------------------------------------
🧩 1. Using Collections.synchronizedList():

public class SyncListExample{
public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException{
List<Integer> list=Collections.synchronizedList(new ArrayList<>());

//Thread 1
Thread t1=new Thread(()->{
for(int i=1;i<=5;i++){
list.add(i);
sout("Thread added:"+ i));
}
});

//thread 2
Thread t2=new Thread(()->{
for(int i=6;i<=10;i++){
list.add(i);
sout("Thread 2 added:"+ i);
}
});
)

t1.start();
t2.start();

t1.join();
t2.join();
sout("final list: "+ list);
}
}

//synchronizedList → locks everything (one at a time)
  CopyOnWriteArrayList → makes copy → no conflict
  Vector → old version of synchronized list